1
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:07,679
Last time, we asked:

2
00:00:07,699 --> 00:00:08,719
A tadpole!

3
00:00:09,019 --> 00:00:11,329
It lives in water, and it has a tail.

4
00:00:11,619 --> 00:00:12,989
What will it grow into?

5
00:00:13,041 --> 00:00:14,131
One, a fish.

6
00:00:15,381 --> 00:00:16,451
Two, a frog.

7
00:00:17,671 --> 00:00:19,001
Three, a lizard.

8
00:00:20,478 --> 00:00:21,988
Hold on to your answer!

9
00:00:23,860 --> 00:00:26,620
A little tree frog is hiding in this video.

10
00:00:26,870 --> 00:00:28,110
Can you spot it?

11
00:00:28,233 --> 00:00:31,163
Tree frogs have sticky toes, so they climb up high.

12
00:00:31,403 --> 00:00:33,583
Look on the leaves, not just in the water!

13
00:00:33,629 --> 00:00:35,089
You against the Buddies!

14
00:00:35,359 --> 00:00:37,209
Lock in first with your fingers.

15
00:00:37,479 --> 00:00:39,309
One finger for every point.

16
00:00:39,890 --> 00:00:41,040
Today you'll learn:

17
00:00:41,241 --> 00:00:43,041
The 3-stage life cycle.

18
00:00:43,246 --> 00:00:44,676
Young that look different.

19
00:00:44,881 --> 00:00:46,551
Why frog eggs have jelly.

20
00:00:47,056 --> 00:00:47,996
Are you ready?

21
00:00:48,436 --> 00:00:49,206
Three!

22
00:00:49,586 --> 00:00:50,246
Two!

23
00:00:50,616 --> 00:00:51,266
One!

24
00:00:51,686 --> 00:00:52,406
Go!

25
00:00:53,795 --> 00:00:54,685
Round one!

26
00:00:54,995 --> 00:00:56,775
What will the tadpole grow into?

27
00:00:57,065 --> 00:00:58,375
Show me your fingers!

28
00:01:01,844 --> 00:01:02,824
Locked in!

29
00:01:02,952 --> 00:01:06,652
One. It lives in water and swims with a tail, just like a

30
00:01:06,672 --> 00:01:07,512
fish.

31
00:01:07,562 --> 00:01:08,302
Three!

32
00:01:08,402 --> 00:01:11,042
It has a long tail like me, so it must grow into

33
00:01:11,062 --> 00:01:12,422
a handsome lizard!

34
00:01:12,473 --> 00:01:13,263
Two.

35
00:01:13,343 --> 00:01:16,293
Frogs sing at this pond every night, so I think it grows

36
00:01:16,313 --> 00:01:17,473
into a frog.

37
00:01:17,749 --> 00:01:19,768
But where do the tadpoles come from?

38
00:01:19,788 --> 00:01:20,628
I know!

39
00:01:20,778 --> 00:01:24,798
A mother frog has baby tadpoles, just like my mum had kittens!

40
00:01:25,452 --> 00:01:26,582
Look closer.

41
00:01:27,212 --> 00:01:30,632
Among the lily pads is a clump of clear jelly, full of

42
00:01:30,652 --> 00:01:32,127
tiny dark dots.

43
00:01:32,147 --> 00:01:33,587
Each dark dot is an egg!

44
00:01:33,777 --> 00:01:36,060
So the mother frog lays eggs, in the water.

45
00:01:36,080 --> 00:01:39,020
But why are the eggs inside all this slippery jelly?

46
00:01:39,067 --> 00:01:42,017
Frog eggs have a jelly-like covering.

47
00:01:42,587 --> 00:01:46,527
The covering protects the eggs from being eaten by other animals.

48
00:01:47,107 --> 00:01:49,607
It also keeps the eggs from drying out.

49
00:01:50,731 --> 00:01:53,751
The jelly is slippery, so a hungry fish finds it hard to

50
00:01:53,771 --> 00:01:54,701
grab an egg.

51
00:01:55,011 --> 00:01:57,301
And it holds water, so the eggs stay wet!

52
00:01:59,923 --> 00:02:01,073
Be a frog egg!

53
00:02:01,383 --> 00:02:02,373
Shrink down.

54
00:02:02,653 --> 00:02:03,583
Quietly.

55
00:02:05,870 --> 00:02:09,240
You are a tiny egg, inside the soft, clear jelly.

56
00:02:10,010 --> 00:02:12,330
A fish swims by, but you are safe.

57
00:02:12,836 --> 00:02:14,066
Days go by.

58
00:02:14,846 --> 00:02:16,526
You wriggle out of the jelly.

59
00:02:17,306 --> 00:02:20,836
You are a tadpole, with a round body and a long tail!

60
00:02:21,359 --> 00:02:22,589
Weeks go by.

61
00:02:23,359 --> 00:02:26,579
Two back legs grow out, and then two front legs.

62
00:02:27,100 --> 00:02:28,700
Your tail shrinks away.

63
00:02:29,490 --> 00:02:32,630
You climb onto a lily pad, and you breathe the air.

64
00:02:33,410 --> 00:02:34,650
You are a frog!

65
00:02:36,374 --> 00:02:38,344
The answer is two: a frog!

66
00:02:38,634 --> 00:02:39,674
Two fingers?

67
00:02:39,944 --> 00:02:41,154
One finger up!

68
00:02:41,205 --> 00:02:43,785
The young of the frog is called a tadpole.

69
00:02:44,975 --> 00:02:46,795
A tadpole is a young frog.

70
00:02:46,875 --> 00:02:49,925
It grew legs, and its tail shrank away, so now it hops

71
00:02:49,945 --> 00:02:51,085
like its parents!

72
00:02:51,137 --> 00:02:52,407
It lives in water.

73
00:02:52,717 --> 00:02:55,547
It has a tail and does not look like the adult.

74
00:02:56,278 --> 00:02:57,358
My turn!

75
00:02:57,598 --> 00:03:01,848
I drew every change: egg, tadpole, tadpole with legs, and frog.

76
00:03:02,048 --> 00:03:03,768
That is four stages!

77
00:03:03,892 --> 00:03:05,452
Something is not right.

78
00:03:05,722 --> 00:03:07,902
If you can spot it, cross your arms.

79
00:03:08,182 --> 00:03:09,142
Hold on!

80
00:03:14,555 --> 00:03:15,685
Arms crossed?

81
00:03:15,955 --> 00:03:17,165
One finger up!

82
00:03:17,217 --> 00:03:19,247
A tadpole with legs is still the young.

83
00:03:19,417 --> 00:03:22,247
It is still growing into the adult, so the frog has three

84
00:03:22,267 --> 00:03:23,287
stages!

85
00:03:26,033 --> 00:03:27,193
Say it with me!

86
00:03:27,899 --> 00:03:31,449
A life cycle with three stages includes the egg, the young and

87
00:03:31,469 --> 00:03:32,439
the adult.

88
00:03:35,062 --> 00:03:38,274
Does every young animal look so different from its parents?

89
00:03:38,294 --> 00:03:39,984
Look, a hen and her chicks!

90
00:03:40,264 --> 00:03:43,327
Some chickens walk freely near HDB blocks.

91
00:03:43,347 --> 00:03:45,267
Those chicks look nothing like the hen!

92
00:03:45,427 --> 00:03:48,777
They are small, yellow and fluffy, and she is big and brown.

93
00:03:49,432 --> 00:03:50,562
Look closer.

94
00:03:51,172 --> 00:03:52,902
Do not look only at the colour.

95
00:03:53,502 --> 00:03:54,915
Look at the body parts.

96
00:03:54,935 --> 00:03:57,725
The chick has a beak, two wings and two legs, just like

97
00:03:57,745 --> 00:03:58,435
the hen.

98
00:03:58,455 --> 00:04:00,935
And it pecks at the ground, just like its mum.

99
00:04:01,085 --> 00:04:03,200
It is a smaller, fluffier copy!

100
00:04:03,220 --> 00:04:06,030
The young of the chicken is called a chick.

101
00:04:07,420 --> 00:04:08,080
Oops!

102
00:04:08,210 --> 00:04:09,530
I only looked at the colour.

103
00:04:09,750 --> 00:04:12,290
A chick looks like the adult, the way a kitten looks like

104
00:04:12,310 --> 00:04:13,180
a cat!

105
00:04:16,877 --> 00:04:18,127
Say it with me!

106
00:04:18,837 --> 00:04:22,017
Some animals have three stages in their life cycles.

107
00:04:22,637 --> 00:04:25,727
Some of the young animals look like their parents, while some do

108
00:04:25,747 --> 00:04:26,467
not.

109
00:04:28,945 --> 00:04:30,405
Show me your score hand!

110
00:04:30,685 --> 00:04:32,075
One finger or more?

111
00:04:32,395 --> 00:04:33,755
You beat the Buddies.

112
00:04:34,025 --> 00:04:35,055
Two fingers?

113
00:04:35,335 --> 00:04:36,345
High five!

114
00:04:36,917 --> 00:04:38,607
Did you spot the tree frog?

115
00:04:38,877 --> 00:04:41,497
It was on the garden tap, beside the pond!

116
00:04:41,627 --> 00:04:43,107
Here is a fun fact!

117
00:04:43,167 --> 00:04:46,287
This tree frog lays its eggs in a ball of foam, on

118
00:04:46,307 --> 00:04:47,697
a leaf above the pond.

119
00:04:47,737 --> 00:04:50,547
When the tadpoles hatch, they drop into the water!

120
00:04:50,674 --> 00:04:51,954
Tell someone at home!

121
00:04:52,683 --> 00:04:54,883
Let's read today's key words together!

122
00:04:55,173 --> 00:04:55,933
Ready?

123
00:04:56,220 --> 00:04:57,650
Jelly-like covering.

124
00:04:59,465 --> 00:05:00,325
Tadpole.

125
00:05:01,694 --> 00:05:02,424
Chick.

126
00:05:03,690 --> 00:05:04,630
Well done!

127
00:05:05,427 --> 00:05:08,317
Look! A little grasshopper with no wings.

128
00:05:08,337 --> 00:05:11,101
And what is this empty grasshopper on the grass?

129
00:05:11,121 --> 00:05:12,711
Find out in Part Two!

130
00:05:13,871 --> 00:05:14,972
Say it with us!

131
00:05:15,772 --> 00:05:16,522
Ready?

132
00:05:16,645 --> 00:05:17,305
One!

133
00:05:17,645 --> 00:05:18,345
two!

134
00:05:18,650 --> 00:05:19,825
Now you know!
